### Exemplary Patent Language

An electrical power system comprising:

- an alternator **(1)** mechanically coupled to a drive system **(7)** and configured to generate electrical power;
- an alternator output bus **(10)** electrically coupled to an output of the alternator **(1)**;
- a reversible converter **(2)** electrically coupled to the alternator output bus **(10)** and operable to transfer electrical energy bidirectionally;
- an AC bus **(6)** coupled to an alternating-current side of the reversible converter **(2)**;
- a DC bus **(9)** coupled to a direct-current side of the reversible converter **(2)**;
- a storage element **(3)** electrically coupled to the DC bus **(9)** and configured selectively to store electrical energy received through the reversible converter **(2)** and to supply stored electrical energy through the reversible converter **(2)**; and
- a controller **(4)** operatively coupled to at least the reversible converter **(2)** and the drive system **(7)**, the controller **(4)** being configured to control a direction and magnitude of power transfer among the alternator **(1)**, the storage element **(3)**, the AC bus **(6)**, and the DC bus **(9)**.

The controller **(4)** may be further configured to operate the reversible converter **(2)** in a first operating mode in which electrical energy generated by the alternator **(1)** is supplied via the alternator output bus **(10)** to one or both of the AC bus **(6)** and the storage element **(3)**, and in a second operating mode in which electrical energy from the storage element **(3)** is transferred via the DC bus **(9)** and the reversible converter **(2)** to the AC bus **(6)** and/or the alternator output bus **(10)**.
